* =====================================================================
*  SPICE model for Lite-On LTST-C171KRKT
*  AlInGaP Red SMD LED (0805 / 2.0 x 1.25 mm), water-clear lens
*  Datasheet: LITE-ON DS22-2000-109, Rev. I (11/09/2023)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*  Key datasheet ratings (Ta = 25 C):
*    Vf            : 1.5 (min) .. 2.4 (max) V  @ If = 20 mA
*    If (DC)       : 25 mA max
*    If (peak)     : 60 mA  (1/10 duty, 0.1 ms pulse)
*    Vr            : 5 V max
*    Ir            : 10 uA max @ Vr = 5 V
*    Pd            : 62.5 mW
*    Peak wavelen. : 639 nm  -> Eg ~= 1.94 eV
*    Dominant wl.  : 624 .. 638 nm
*    Viewing angle : 130 deg
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*  Model derivation (Shockley diode + series resistance):
*    Fit to Fig.2 (If vs Vf) at two operating points:
*       ~1.0 mA @ 1.82 V   and   20 mA @ 2.00 V
*    chosen RS = 3.5 ohm to match the ~5 ohm dynamic slope (20->30 mA),
*    giving N = 1.5 and IS = 3.57e-24 A.
*    Spot checks:  20 mA -> 2.00 V,  25 mA -> 2.03 V,  1 mA -> 1.85 V.
*    BV/IBV encode the 10 uA @ 5 V reverse-leakage spec.
*    EG/XTI set for AlInGaP for realistic temperature dependence.
* =====================================================================

.MODEL LTST-C171KRKT D
+ ( IS=3.57e-24   ; saturation current  [A]
+   N=1.5         ; emission coefficient (ideality factor)
+   RS=3.5        ; series resistance    [ohm]
+   CJO=30p       ; zero-bias junction capacitance [F]
+   VJ=0.75       ; junction potential   [V]
+   M=0.33        ; grading coefficient
+   BV=5          ; reverse "breakdown"/rating voltage [V]
+   IBV=10u       ; current at BV (encodes 10 uA @ 5 V spec) [A]
+   EG=1.94       ; bandgap energy (AlInGaP red) [eV]
+   XTI=3 )       ; IS temperature exponent

* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*  Usage example (LTspice):
*    Place a "diode" symbol, set Value = LTST-C171KRKT,
*    and add this file via a .include / .lib directive, e.g.:
*       .lib LTST-C171KRKT.lib
*
*    D1  anode  cathode  LTST-C171KRKT
*
*  Drive at the rated 20 mA from a 5 V rail:
*    Rseries = (5 V - 2.0 V) / 20 mA = 150 ohm
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*  Notes:
*   - Forward characteristics are the focus; reverse leakage in real
*     parts is dominated by surface effects, so this model is typically
*     "better than" the 10 uA worst-case spec below 5 V.
*   - This is an ELECTRICAL model only (no optical/luminous output).
* =====================================================================
